  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Public Service i praktiken</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public service broadcasting in practice</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Swedish Radio Media Development Organisation will support five regional radio stations under Rwanda Broadcasting Agency and  their youth station in Kigali as well as four independent community radios, all in their given mandates. SR MDO will complete what they had to suspend 2015 upon Sidas termination of agreement with IWPR in Rwanda as the organisation was denied the right to register. The agreement with IWPR is cancelled.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Syftet &#xe4;r att bidra till att st&#xe4;rka fem regionala public service radiostationer och en station f&#xf6;r unga via Rwanda Broadcasting Agency samt fyra oberoende byradiostationer i Rwanda genom coaching av Sveriges Radio Media Development Organisation (SR MDO). Radio stationerna ska st&#xe4;rkas i den uppgift de &#xe4;r &#xe5;lagda att genomf&#xf6;ra. SR MDO kommer att slutf&#xf6;ra vad de p&#xe5;b&#xf6;rjade 2015 inom ett st&#xf6;rre mediaprogram som ej kunde slutf&#xf6;ras d&#xe5; avtalspartnern, IWPR, f&#xf6;rlorade sin registrering i landet. Avtalet med IWPR &#xe4;r nu uppsagt.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective has been to contribute to strengthened freedom of expression in Rwanda and support a clear role of broadcasting media as a tool of democracy and empowerment of the citizens.
Firstly, during the 1,5 year long project the Swedish Radio Media Development Organisation (SR-MDO) aimed at contributing to the transformation of Rwanda Broadcasting Agency&#x2019;s regional radio stations into Public Service Radios, delivering more professional programming, news and current affairs programmes in line with International Journalistic Standards and Public Service Broadcasting Values.Secondly, RBA&#x2019;s Magic FM in Kigali established as a station for urban youth delivering programs and content according to Public Service Broadcasting Values.
Thirdly the project aimed at supporting a five year strategic plan for RBA to be developed, including clarity and commitment at Board and Executive level regarding role of Public Service Broadcasting in Rwanda and clarity for the boards and the executive of their role and responsibility and having established procedures and policies for good.</narrative>
  </description>
